id: pm-web-onv4
title: Server hangs/cryptic error when DATABASE_URL is unset
description: "SYMPTOM: Starting pm-web without DATABASE_URL produced no output for several seconds, then a cryptic 'getaddrinfo EAI_AGAIN pm-telemetry-postgres' DNS error. db.ts silently fell back to a hardcoded telemetry-specific host (pm-telemetry-postgres) with undefined credentials, and the failure only surfaced after the 5s pool connectionTimeout. REPRO: env -u DATABASE_URL node dist/server.js  (observed ~5s silent wait then DNS error stack). EXPECTED: a server that requires a DB should fail fast with a clear actionable message and exit non-zero. OBSERVED vs EXPECTED: cryptic delayed DNS error vs clear 'DATABASE_URL is not set' guidance. FIX: added assertDbConfigured() in db.ts (validates DATABASE_URL or POSTGRES_HOST+POSTGRES_DB, removed the pm-telemetry-postgres default), called at the top of server.ts before any DB use; also collapsed the schema-init catch to print err.message instead of a full stack. Now: no DATABASE_URL -> instant clear message + exit 1 (1s); unreachable DB -> clean one-line timeout error + exit 1."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-05-29T15:44:53.057Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T16:56:36.288Z"
author: codex
parent: pm-web-ul0n
comments[27]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T10:00:09.069Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed the missing-database guard is hidden by generic error redaction. Plan: value-free startup validation before binding, database configuration/reachability/schema doctor check, built-process regressions, and explicit plain-directory SDK acceptance."
  "2026-10-20T10:10:10.720Z",codex-agent,"Built-process doctor and no-git acceptance passed (2/2): database missing/unreachable/schema-missing/current diagnostics, read-only schema inspection, and SDK create/get/update/list with no git executable. Restoring the old startup guard made both foreground diagnostic regressions fail (0/2), exit 1, after rebuilding; full revert receipts follow."
  "2026-10-20T10:11:15.039Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: restored only the old startup guard placement and generic logging, rebuilt, then node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern=\"foreground built|built server reports every invalid\" test/startup-readiness.test.ts failed 2/2 (exit 1). Restored fixed sources and rebuilt."
  "2026-10-20T10:21:04.858Z",codex-agent,"Final focused linked run passed 9/9 (exit 0), including explicit tracker-path isolation under pm test. Existing result tracking is disabled; receipt recorded here. Startup/revert evidence is documented in docs/startup-readiness.md."
  "2026-10-20T10:26:39.191Z",codex-agent,"Additional doctor edge case confirmed: PostgreSQL client construction can throw before connecting when DATABASE_URL names a missing certificate. Moved client construction inside the redacted diagnostic catch and added a real doctor-process regression ensuring the certificate value is not emitted. Final gates will cover this hardened version."
  "2026-10-20T10:31:52.028Z",codex-agent,Doctor certificate-value regression passes 1/1. Behavioral revert moving only client construction back outside the catch fails the same process regression 0/1 (exit 1); fixed sources restored and rebuilt. The broad npm gate has reproduced the existing built-catalog 300-second timeout and following source-case failure documented in pm-web-qdhx; startup regressions and full gate results will be reported separately.
  "2026-10-20T10:44:39.915Z",codex-agent,"Final hardened implementation passes the full linked startup suite 9/9, zero failures/cancellations/skips, exit 0. This rerun includes missing-certificate client construction. The current broad npm suite separately reproduces known catalog timing failures (pm-web-qdhx) and the unchanged large-corpus graph latency assertion (pm-web-hqqp); no thresholds or deadlines were relaxed."
  "2026-10-20T11:00:41.628Z",codex-agent,"The broad gate exposed an implementation-layout assertion requiring assertOidcConfiguration literally in server.ts. Replaced that assertion with reliance on the existing real-process OIDC refusal test, preserving behavior before binding. Added the revision marker to the shipped SQL schema too, and extended real doctor acceptance to a database initialized from sql/schema.sql."
  "2026-10-20T11:04:56.921Z",codex-agent,"SQL-initialized doctor acceptance, the OIDC contract and real-process OIDC startup refusal pass 3/3. Restoring only the original packaged SQL without its revision marker makes the doctor regression fail 0/1 (exit 1); fixed SQL restored. Runtime/schema test expectations retain all existing deadlines and numeric gate thresholds."
  "2026-10-20T11:07:32.646Z",codex-agent,Removing only startup log redaction makes the supporting privacy unit fail 0/1 (exit 1); fixed code restored. The preliminary broad gate was interrupted after its known timing failures and the now-corrected OIDC layout assertion so clean final-code npm and Bun runs can start without overlapping development tests. No interrupted result is accepted as a passing gate.
  "2026-10-20T12:06:26.191Z",codex-agent,"Completed final-code npm attempt: 696 tests, 692 pass, 3 fail, 1 canceled, 0 skipped. Timing failures: catalog deadline/cascade, 2000-item graph read 27732ms against unchanged 10000ms, and fatal-output child SIGTERM at its unchanged 10s deadline. Coverage was 91.58 statements/lines, 81.19 branches, 95.35 functions; line/statement floor92.07 remained unmet. Built-only detached helper execution was not counted in source coverage, so added source contract tests using real built child processes and real PostgreSQL. No thresholds or source scope changed."
  "2026-10-20T12:21:05.869Z",codex-agent,"Focused source contract tests for database diagnostics and detached lifecycle pass against real processes/PostgreSQL, measuring 100 statements/lines/functions for each new helper. Reverting only the source helper to immediate spawn success fails 0/1; reverting only database readiness to blind success fails 0/1. Both implementations restored. The unchanged fatal-output tests pass focused 2/2, contrasting with the 10-second full-coverage deadline failure."
  "2026-10-20T12:37:24.779Z",codex-agent,"Final linked startup suite passes 13/13, source lifecycle selection passes 1/1, and oversized-log privacy selection passes 1/1. Direct configured/discrete/unreachable/certificate diagnostics use real PostgreSQL. The API-key redaction assertion also passes; disabling redaction still fails 0/1. All reversions restored before final gates."
  "2026-10-20T13:54:56.956Z",codex-agent,"Preserved PostgreSQL URLs whose host is supplied through the query (including socket-directory form). Real PostgreSQL accepts this form. Fixed configuration, source doctor and built-child startup selections pass 3/3; reverting only host-query support and rebuilding fails all 3/3, then the implementation was restored and rebuilt. The built doctor also verifies the packaged SQL schema marker without mutating an empty database."
  "2026-10-20T14:49:16.920Z",codex-agent,"Final frozen-input release checks PASS, both exit 0. npm: 699/699 tests, coverage statements/lines 92.61, branches 81.55, functions 95.97. Bun: 699/699, coverage statements/lines 92.65, branches 81.63, functions 95.97. Both report all 44 required sources, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo, capacity 2/2, packed consumers 4/4, audit zero vulnerabilities and all typecheck/lint/duplication/docstring/package/changelog/release checks. All 393 runtime/test/schema/build inputs stayed unchanged; thresholds and deadlines are unchanged. Latest linked startup suite passes 13/13. Evidence and all 11 behavioral revert proofs (18 selected failing cases across the reverts) are in docs/startup-readiness.md. Claims will be released and items left open."
  "2026-10-20T15:44:52.630Z",codex-agent,"PR #230 review round: fetched current branch and main; branch already contains main. Read all comments on both unresolved review threads PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6uZXBh and PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6uZXB1; latest CodeRabbit body has no Outside diff range findings. Verified empty DATABASE_URL and omitted database-path incompatibilities, non-production OIDC soft-disable regression, and premature foreground banner. Reuse this item for fixes, behavioral revert proofs and unchanged npm/Bun release gates. No review replies or thread resolution."
  "2026-10-20T15:47:18.080Z",codex-agent,"Implemented both valid review findings and foreground banner ordering. DATABASE_URL uses the same truthiness guard as pool/doctor, omitted database paths use pg defaults, and whitespace-only URLs remain invalid rather than silently selecting discrete settings. OIDC soft-disable remains nonfatal outside production. Foreground checks the shared preflight before its Starting/Ctrl+C lines. Focused fixed selection passes 4/4 with real PostgreSQL and built child processes. Whole PR diff reviewed for configuration-policy divergence and premature success output; detached started output already follows child-owned readiness. Four isolated behavioral reverts are running before final linked/full gates."
  "2026-10-20T15:47:55.302Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs, fixed tests unchanged, each rebuilt with npm run build:server: (1) only DATABASE_URL guard reverted to !== undefined: database preflight selection fails 0/1, exit 1; (2) only mandatory pathname check restored: same selection fails 0/1, exit 1; (3) only non-production OIDC issue restored: OIDC preflight selection fails 0/1, exit 1; (4) only foreground preflight-before-banner block removed: foreground built|real CLI selection fails 0/2, exit 1, including actual pm web --json in a non-git temp tracker. Failures are assertion failures for the intended defects, not timeouts. Restored all fixed source and rebuilt after each proof. Exact selections: node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern=\"database preflight\" test/startup-readiness.test.ts; replace pattern with \"OIDC preflight\" or \"foreground built|real CLI\" for the other proofs. Final linked suite and unchanged release gates follow."
  "2026-10-20T15:54:17.936Z",codex-agent,"Self-review found another instance of runtime/preflight divergence: empty optional PORT and PM_WEB_DB_POOL_MAX values use runtime defaults but fail startup validation; empty POSTGRES_PORT uses the pool default but fails the shared database validator, and doctor uses a different fallback expression. Empty environment startup timeout also needs the same default at the launcher and preflight. Align default selection while keeping explicit invalid CLI values and nonempty invalid numeric settings rejected. Add source-level defaults coverage and real built detached startup with empty optional settings, then behavioral reverts before the final frozen-input gates. Initial linked run reached its 120-second outer pm runner timeout with zero assertion failures; rerun uses --timeout 600 without changing repository deadlines."
  "2026-10-20T15:57:24.243Z",codex-agent,"Final-code behavioral reverts all fail as intended: empty DATABASE_URL guard 0/1; required URL pathname 0/1; non-production OIDC fatal policy 0/1; foreground preflight removal 0/2. Additional numeric reverts each fail 0/1: startupConfigIssues nullish instead of empty-as-unset defaults, postgresPort nullish fallback, and launcher timeout nullish fallback. Every revert rebuilt dist, exited 1 with intended assertion failures and zero timeouts/cancellations/skips; all fixed sources restored and rebuilt. Numeric selection command: node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern=\"empty optional numeric\" test/startup-readiness.test.ts. Fixed numeric direct run passes 1/1. Earlier linked full suite passed 16/16 on retry with --timeout 600 (default outer 120-second timeout interrupted the initial run); the newly added numeric case follows as a linked selection. Strict tracker validation passes; strict health separately reports existing pm-github host-version skew and stale active items. No pin changes or history repairs."
  "2026-10-20T16:01:09.061Z",codex-agent,"First full npm gate stopped at the unchanged zero-duplication threshold: two repeated assertion blocks in the new tests (8 duplicated lines). Refactored shared built-child readiness assertions into a documented fixture helper, retaining exit/status/HTTP/JSON assertions and the existing parent-exit/live-pidfile checks. Production code is unchanged by this test refactor. Repeat all seven behavioral reverts against the final tests, then rerun npm and Bun full release gates. No thresholds or deadlines relaxed."
  "2026-10-20T16:03:41.802Z",codex-agent,"Final test refactor clears duplication at 0% (zero clone pairs). Repeated all seven behavioral reverts against these exact tests: six single-test selections fail 0/1 each and the foreground built|real CLI selection fails 0/2, all exit 1 from intended assertions with zero timeouts/cancellations/skips. Restored final code and rebuilt committed dist. Restarted full npm then Bun release checks sequentially with fresh HOME and disabled global/system Git config, recording hashes of 261 runtime/test/build inputs and checking for drift after each gate. Thresholds, source scope and repository deadlines remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-20T16:13:55.527Z",codex-agent,"Current npm full run reproduces the previously tracked catalog 300-second timeout and subsequent source-case failure under heavy shared-host load (pm-web-qdhx); it is continuing to collect the rest of the suite. Typecheck, lint, zero-duplication and 764 documented declarations pass. All seven final behavioral revert proofs are complete. Push the concrete fixes with this evidence so the existing CI can verify both complete npm and Bun release gates on Node 22 and 26 independently of local load. Keep all existing deadlines, thresholds and dependency pins unchanged. Gate completion and CI results will be recorded before the final handoff."
  "2026-10-20T16:28:08.151Z",codex-agent,"CI source-head run 39455980587 completed both npm suites: 703 tests, 702 passed, 1 failed, zero cancellations/skips. Catalog and graph timing failures from the overloaded local host pass in CI. The sole genuine failure is an existing bootstrap assertion expecting generic child exit for an empty JWT secret; preflight now correctly refuses before spawn. Updated that assertion to require the actionable configuration error, then restore the valid secret before the separate source-wrapper missing-child scenario so child-failure coverage remains intact. Node 22 also missed the unchanged function floor because the early assertion aborted the rest of this lifecycle test. Interrupted only the superseded local gate process group after recording its catalog/graph timing failures. Focused validation and another bootstrap revert proof precede the next CI full gates."
  "2026-10-20T16:32:14.862Z",codex-agent,"Corrected bootstrap lifecycle selection passes 1/1 directly and 1/1 through pm test --run --progress --only-last --timeout 600. It separately proves actionable missing-JWT refusal and a real numeric missing-child error after restoring valid signing configuration. New behavioral revert: removed only the foreground preflight block, rebuilt, and ran node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern=\"the extension starts, probes\" test/server-bootstrap.test.ts; failed 0/1 with exit 1 on the intended preflight-error assertion, no timeout/cancellation/skip. Restored fixed code and rebuilt; production source/dist match 4fbead1. Total this round: 8 independent behavioral reverts, 9 intended failing cases. Duplication remains 0% and test TypeScript build passes. Push the assertion correction for full Node 22/26 npm and Bun CI gates."
  "2026-10-20T16:45:17.615Z",codex-agent,"Updated head 9415541 passes both complete npm release gates in CI on Node 22 and 26, including the corrected bootstrap lifecycle test and all unchanged coverage floors. CI run 39458568307 has advanced beyond those gates to its additional packed-consumer acceptance; full Bun release gates are next. CodeQL also passes on this head. The earlier local catalog timeout/cascade and graph latency failures pass in CI without changing source, deadlines or thresholds."
  "2026-10-20T16:56:31.355Z",codex-agent,"FINAL release evidence: CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/39458568307 on source head 9415541 passes full npm run release:check AND bun run release:check on Node 22 and 26. Each of all four gates: 703/703 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo, all 44 sources, capacity 2/2, packed npm/native-Bun current/minimum consumers 4/4, audit zero vulnerabilities, duplication 0%, 764 documented declarations, and every remaining release check passed. Coverage statements/lines/branches/functions: Node22 npm 92.63/92.63/81.69/95.12; Node22 Bun 92.66/92.66/81.71/95.12; Node26 npm 92.61/92.61/81.64/95.98; Node26 Bun 92.63/92.63/81.69/95.98. Thresholds and deadlines unchanged. CI strict tracker health, fresh committed-dist check and CodeQL pass. Local catalog timeout/cascade and graph latency failures pass in CI; outer linked timeout passes on retry. Eight behavioral reverts fail 9 intended cases; fixed linked startup 16/16 plus numeric 1/1 and corrected bootstrap 1/1. Full suites include all 17 startup cases. Latest complete review read still contains only the original two unresolved threads and no outside-diff findings. Final update adds evidence and releases the claim only; 261 recorded runtime/test/build inputs and dist remain identical to the tested source head. Local health version skew/stale warnings remain separate. No new pm CLI/SDK defect identified; no review replies/resolutions, merge, release, or hosted changes."
